4. DATASET 003 — HiRISE
==================================================

FULL NAME:
High Resolution Imaging Science Experiment.

SOURCE MISSION:
NASA Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter.

DATA CATEGORY:
High-Resolution Surface Imaging and Terrain Hazard Analysis.

SCIENTIFIC PURPOSE:

HiRISE provides extremely detailed orbital images of Mars.

It supports the study of:

- Small impact craters.
- Boulders.
- Rock formations.
- Sand dunes.
- Surface textures.
- Landing site hazards.
- Geological structures.
- Small-scale terrain features.

DATA CHARACTERISTICS:

- Approximately 25–50 cm per pixel for commonly used image products, depending on acquisition conditions and processing.
- High-resolution targeted imaging.
- Stereo image acquisitions available for selected locations.
- Digital Terrain Models available for selected stereo coverage.

GAME INTEGRATION:

A. Landing Hazard Detection:
Identify visible rocks, craters and potentially hazardous terrain features.

B. Landing Site Assessment:
Provide high-resolution inspection of candidate landing regions.

C. Rover Navigation:
Support detailed terrain analysis when suitable imagery or elevation products are available.

D. Mission Risk:
Flag potentially hazardous terrain.

