6. DATASET 005 — CRISM
==================================================

FULL NAME:
Compact Reconnaissance Imaging Spectrometer for Mars.

SOURCE MISSION:
NASA Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter.

DATA CATEGORY:
Mineralogy and Spectral Geology.

SCIENTIFIC PURPOSE:

CRISM studies the mineral composition of the Martian surface using reflected sunlight and spectral observations.

It helps identify evidence of minerals associated with past water-related processes.

Potential mineralogical targets include:

- Phyllosilicates.
- Hydrated sulfates.
- Carbonates.
- Iron-bearing minerals.
- Other spectrally identifiable surface materials.

DATA CHARACTERISTICS:

TARGETED OBSERVATIONS:
Approximately 18–36 meters per pixel for commonly used targeted products.

SURVEY OBSERVATIONS:
Approximately 90–180 meters per pixel for commonly used products.

DATA TYPES:

- Spectral cubes.
- Mineral identification products.
- Spectral parameter maps.
- Targeted observations.
- Regional mineralogical survey products.

GAME INTEGRATION:

A. Science Mission Design:
Allow players to select mineralogical investigation objectives.

B. Landing Site Selection:
Identify regions with known mineralogical observations.

C. Rover Exploration:
Use orbital mineralogical evidence to identify scientifically interesting destinations.

D. Mission Objectives:
Create mineral collection or mineral investigation objectives.

E. Scientific Results:
Generate mission science reports based on actual available observations and clearly labelled derived interpretations.

VISUALIZATION:

- Mineral distribution map.
- Spectral data visualization.
- Mineral detection overlays.
- Geological investigation markers.
- Science target selection.

IMPORTANT:
Do not treat mineral detections as proof of biological activity or definitive evidence of life.

Do not claim that every location has CRISM coverage.

